Azerbaijani " [:a {:href "/athletes/117109"} "Xetaq Qazyumov"] ". Oddly, in 2012 at London Gogshelidze and Qazyumov would repeat as the bronze medalists in this class."] "\n\n" [:p {} "That was how the event and the results seemed to have ended. In 2015, however, the IOC began re-testing samples from the 2008 Beijing and 2012 London Olympics, using newer, more advanced testing techniques, in an effort to find those who had used performance enhancing drugs (PEDs), but in whom it could not be detected at the time of those Olympics. This was one of the many events affected."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In October 2016, " [:a {:href "/athletes/117108"} "Taymuraz Tigiyev"] " (KAZ) was revealed to have a positive test for turinabol (dehydrochloromethyltestosterone), and was disqualified, losing his silver medal. Georgian " [:a {:href "/athletes/117110"} "Giorgi Gogshelidze"] " was upgraded to a silver medal, while Cuban " [:a {:href "/athletes/117111"} "Michel Batista"] " received the bronze medal. Tigiyev’s brother, " [:a {:href "/athletes/117078"} "Soslan Tigiyev"] ", who competed for Uzbekistan, had also originally won a bronze medal in 74 kg freestyle, but was also disqualified in October 2016 for turinabol."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "12"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/117107"} "Shirvani Muradov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RUS.png"}] "RUS"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/117110"} "Giorgi Gogshelidze"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GEO"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia